      "content": "Start by capturing full environment details, including container images and random seeds, to rule out configuration drift. Enable Jenkins' persistent agent caching to ensure test runners share the exact same underlying state. If flakiness persists despite this, consider rerunning the build in a clean container with explicit environment variables to isolate hardware or library-specific noise.",
